       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. And this dose is five times the labeled maximum, so the potential harm is serious: profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours, so an overdose effect would last a long time and be hard to reverse.\n\nIf the problem is that standard dosing hasn't controlled the patient, there are safer routes:\n\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily.** That's the maximum labeled dose, and I can enter it now if you'd like.\n- **Add or switch agents.** An ACE inhibitor or ARB, a thiazide-like diuretic, or another class is the usual next step when amlodipine 10 mg isn't enough.\n- **Pharmacy and specialist verification.** If the specialist really did recommend 50 mg, pharmacy can contact them directly to confirm. They can also help enter it through a pathway that has the right safeguards, such as monitoring parameters and hold parameters.\n\nDo you want me to enter 10 mg once daily, or hold off until pharmacy has reviewed it?"
